1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
== www.kissasia.co  ==

2
00:00:00,159 --> 00:00:01,159
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:01,159 --> 00:00:02,159
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:02,159 --> 00:00:04,126
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:04,126 --> 00:00:07,326
[Episode 6]

6
00:00:11,807 --> 00:00:14,626
Just how far is he going?

7
00:00:18,075 --> 00:00:19,919
I've been here before.

8
00:00:19,919 --> 00:00:21,567
What? When?

9
00:00:21,567 --> 00:00:23,492
Where is this place, Mr. Kwon?

10
00:00:27,295 --> 00:00:29,263
Wait, a casino?

11
00:00:29,263 --> 00:00:32,323
Chairman Cheon came to a casino
at a time like this?

12
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:35,992
When two people just died
at his construction site?

13
00:00:48,207 --> 00:00:50,826
Chairman, I'm Kwon Tae Seong
from Not Today. I requested an interview.

14
00:00:50,826 --> 00:00:52,726
Wait, just a moment...

15
00:00:53,715 --> 00:00:55,048
Why are you covering my mouth?

16
00:00:55,048 --> 00:00:56,399
Chairman! Just a moment.

17
00:00:56,399 --> 00:00:58,868
Wait, Chairman!

18
00:00:58,868 --> 00:01:00,126
Just a moment.

19
00:01:00,126 --> 00:01:02,392
Just let me in for a moment!

20
00:01:04,059 --> 00:01:05,447
I told you to stop.

21
00:01:05,447 --> 00:01:07,159
Stay put.

22
00:01:19,151 --> 00:01:20,235
Are you okay, Mr. Kwon?

23
00:01:20,235 --> 00:01:21,403
Yeah. You got it, right?

24
00:01:21,403 --> 00:01:23,539
Oh, yes, I got it.

25
00:01:23,539 --> 00:01:26,211
Still, it was worth following him
all the way here.

26
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:29,603
Just coming to a casino
at a time like this is newsworthy.

27
00:01:29,603 --> 00:01:32,275
- That's not enough, though, huh?
- What?

28
00:01:32,275 --> 00:01:35,259
Not everyone at a casino is there to gamble.

29
00:01:35,259 --> 00:01:36,959
We need to catch him actually gambling,

30
00:01:36,959 --> 00:01:39,307
or at least meet him
and get a few words out of him.

31
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:41,007
We came all this way for this.

32
00:01:43,239 --> 00:01:44,239
But how are we supposed to do that?

33
00:01:44,239 --> 00:01:47,175
They don't even look like they'll let us
take one step inside, do they?

34
00:01:47,175 --> 00:01:49,226
Is this the only way in?

35
00:01:53,327 --> 00:01:55,426
Go through the lobby,
pass the bell desk on the left,

36
00:01:55,426 --> 00:01:57,692
and open the door on the right.

37
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:01,959
There should be a staff-only elevator.

38
00:02:07,192 --> 00:02:09,626
Take it to the maid's room on B3

39
00:02:10,375 --> 00:02:12,759
and get a master key for the rooms.

40
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,139
Could I ask you a favor?

41
00:02:16,139 --> 00:02:18,126
Of course, I have to help.

42
00:02:18,126 --> 00:02:21,783
You're investigating a case
involving an unjust death, after all.

43
00:02:21,783 --> 00:02:27,271
Your article helped us a lot when we were
fighting wrongful dismissal last year.

44
00:02:27,271 --> 00:02:30,295
Come this way, through the back door.
Come with me.

45
00:02:33,631 --> 00:02:35,726
Excuse me.

46
00:02:37,826 --> 00:02:39,959
Doors closing.

47
00:02:43,603 --> 00:02:45,275
What floor?

48
00:02:45,275 --> 00:02:47,723
B3, the parking garage.

49
00:02:47,723 --> 00:02:49,592
This is for staff only.

50
00:02:49,592 --> 00:02:53,759
You'll have to go back up to the first floor
and take the elevator outside.

51
00:02:53,759 --> 00:02:55,426
Oh, okay. Got it. I'm sorry.

52
00:02:55,426 --> 00:02:57,126
Oh, okay.

53
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:03,992
Doors closing.

54
00:03:11,147 --> 00:03:12,727
Looks like you won't
need to go to the maid room.

55
00:03:12,727 --> 00:03:15,259
Just go straight up to the 23rd floor.

56
00:03:21,063 --> 00:03:23,492
Reporting with you...

57
00:03:24,303 --> 00:03:26,392
is always thrilling.

58
00:03:30,023 --> 00:03:32,526
You'll get used to it eventually.

59
00:03:33,278 --> 00:03:36,692
It seems like it'll be
hard to go up unnoticed.

60
00:03:36,692 --> 00:03:40,526
There are two maids on B1
and two more on the first floor.

61
00:03:40,526 --> 00:03:42,126
Just avoid showing your face
as much as possible.

62
00:03:42,126 --> 00:03:43,359
I'll delete the footage right away.

63
00:03:43,359 --> 00:03:45,092
Okay.

64
00:04:10,679 --> 00:04:13,292
- Doors closing.
- Why is it so exhausting today?

65
00:04:14,035 --> 00:04:15,226
I don't know why there's
so much going on today.

66
00:04:15,226 --> 00:04:17,103
Seriously, why is there so darn much work?

67
00:04:17,103 --> 00:04:18,803
I'm exhausted.

68
00:04:19,731 --> 00:04:22,859
Oh? You're VIP guests.

69
00:04:22,859 --> 00:04:25,435
Oh, I think you got on the wrong elevator.

70
00:04:25,435 --> 00:04:26,659
What?

71
00:04:26,659 --> 00:04:30,059
Next time, use the VIP elevator
on the other side of the hall.

72
00:04:30,059 --> 00:04:32,326
This one's for staff.

73
00:04:32,326 --> 00:04:34,379
Oh, I see.

74
00:04:34,379 --> 00:04:36,499
Thank you.

75
00:04:36,499 --> 00:04:38,199
You too, ma'am.

76
00:04:49,892 --> 00:04:52,392
[Yul's Daycare]

77
00:05:11,507 --> 00:05:14,326
Excuse me, I'm getting off.

78
00:05:29,467 --> 00:05:32,011
What's wrong?

79
00:05:32,011 --> 00:05:34,271
Huh?

80
00:05:34,271 --> 00:05:35,579
Never mind.

81
00:05:35,579 --> 00:05:37,992
Her back just looked like someone.

82
00:05:39,155 --> 00:05:40,363
What a crazy punk.

83
00:05:40,363 --> 00:05:42,959
No, I mean, me.

84
00:05:48,715 --> 00:05:51,007
Yes, Miss. How are you?

85
00:05:51,007 --> 00:05:54,415
Sorry, I couldn't answer your call.
What is it about?

86
00:05:54,415 --> 00:05:56,563
Oh, it's nothing serious.

87
00:05:56,563 --> 00:05:59,203
I'm calling about Yul's first-semester
parent consultation.

88
00:05:59,203 --> 00:06:02,535
You didn't reply in the app to let us know

89
00:06:02,535 --> 00:06:05,249
whether you'd prefer a phone
or in-person consultation.

90
00:06:05,249 --> 00:06:10,715
Oh, sorry. I missed that.
Well, I'll do the in-person consultation.

91
00:06:10,715 --> 00:06:13,926
Yes, thank you, Miss. Yes.

92
00:06:17,959 --> 00:06:20,903
Yeah, I'll take the stairs from here.

93
00:06:20,903 --> 00:06:22,907
Watch for anyone coming in.

94
00:06:22,907 --> 00:06:24,811
We can't have any more witnesses.

95
00:06:24,811 --> 00:06:27,459
Okay, Ms. Yoo, I'll keep a close watch.

96
00:06:34,239 --> 00:06:36,292
How can I help you?

97
00:06:36,292 --> 00:06:39,303
Are you here as a guest?

98
00:06:39,303 --> 00:06:42,703
I'm not here to gamble.
I'm here to meet someone.

99
00:06:42,703 --> 00:06:44,626
Who are you looking for?

100
00:06:45,229 --> 00:06:48,326
Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
of Gaecheon Construction is inside, right?

101
00:06:50,065 --> 00:06:52,643
Did you make an appointment?

102
00:06:52,643 --> 00:06:55,159
He'll know me if you tell him Kwon Tae Seong.

103
00:06:55,857 --> 00:06:59,194
There are guards stationed
on every floor of the VIP rooms.

104
00:06:59,194 --> 00:07:02,019
When I give you the signal,
come out and move to the left.

105
00:07:02,019 --> 00:07:03,719
Okay.

106
00:07:08,735 --> 00:07:10,435
Now!

107
00:07:15,759 --> 00:07:17,826
When's the next shift coming?

108
00:07:36,635 --> 00:07:38,791
I'm in.

109
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:40,491
This is a nice room.

110
00:07:41,123 --> 00:07:43,626
Wow, what a view.

111
00:07:44,959 --> 00:07:46,586
It's annoying, right?

112
00:07:46,586 --> 00:07:48,291
A guy who should be in a prison cell.

113
00:07:48,291 --> 00:07:50,159
I'll head over to the fridge.

114
00:08:19,407 --> 00:08:20,731
- Done.
- Put it back in the fridge

115
00:08:20,731 --> 00:08:22,392
and take everything else out.

116
00:08:22,392 --> 00:08:25,151
Just leave that one bottle of water.

117
00:08:25,151 --> 00:08:27,603
I saw on social media that Tak Jong Gu
is an "iced drink till I die" guy.

118
00:08:27,603 --> 00:08:31,192
What's that?
Something like "a punch in the face"?

119
00:08:33,527 --> 00:08:35,635
Well, that's not bad either.

120
00:08:35,635 --> 00:08:39,192
It means he only drinks iced beverages.

121
00:08:46,291 --> 00:08:47,991
Done.

122
00:08:50,591 --> 00:08:52,291
I'm heading out.

123
00:08:54,223 --> 00:08:55,926
Wait, Ms. Yoo.

124
00:08:57,503 --> 00:09:00,059
Someone's coming down the hall.

125
00:09:00,059 --> 00:09:01,859
Looks like guests.

126
00:09:01,859 --> 00:09:05,143
One man and one woman.

127
00:09:05,143 --> 00:09:06,843
It's Tak Jong Gu.

128
00:09:09,779 --> 00:09:11,703
That woman is...

129
00:09:11,703 --> 00:09:13,826
Huh? A liquor bottle?

130
00:09:15,755 --> 00:09:17,655
First time somewhere this fancy?

131
00:09:17,655 --> 00:09:19,355
Yeah.

132
00:09:20,271 --> 00:09:22,511
Come on in.

133
00:09:22,511 --> 00:09:25,659
- This is my room.
- Wow!

134
00:09:27,179 --> 00:09:29,959
This room is incredible.

135
00:09:32,159 --> 00:09:34,795
You really were born
to the right parents, huh?

136
00:09:34,795 --> 00:09:38,103
Aren't the rooms...

137
00:09:38,103 --> 00:09:39,919
non-smoking?

138
00:09:39,919 --> 00:09:41,727
What's not allowed?

139
00:09:41,727 --> 00:09:45,075
If anyone acts up,
I can just throw money at them.

140
00:09:45,075 --> 00:09:48,492
Man, the more I see you, the more I like you.

141
00:09:52,155 --> 00:09:54,647
That's the woman. Today's variable.

142
00:09:54,647 --> 00:09:58,063
She's the one who snatched
my VIP pass at the gaming room.

143
00:09:58,063 --> 00:09:59,951
What's the variable this time?

144
00:09:59,951 --> 00:10:01,759
I'm not sure about that either...

145
00:10:01,759 --> 00:10:04,067
He's supposed to be stuck
in the gaming room until dawn.

146
00:10:04,067 --> 00:10:06,092
But why are those two here at this hour...

147
00:10:06,987 --> 00:10:10,859
If you stay hidden there,
I'll find a way to get you out.

148
00:10:15,967 --> 00:10:19,311
Won't they figure out we lied right away?

149
00:10:19,311 --> 00:10:20,759
Well, it's not exactly a lie.

150
00:10:20,759 --> 00:10:24,543
I said he'd know my name.
I never said I had an appointment.

151
00:10:24,543 --> 00:10:25,779
Oh!

152
00:10:25,779 --> 00:10:27,626
Here they come. Smile.

153
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:38,071
Chairman Cheon says
he has no appointment today.

154
00:10:38,071 --> 00:10:42,675
Oh, really? That's strange.

155
00:10:43,719 --> 00:10:44,915
He must've forgotten.

156
00:10:44,915 --> 00:10:48,626
Instead of standing here,
perhaps I should speak to him in person...

157
00:10:49,619 --> 00:10:53,559
He's already gone to his room to rest,
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

158
00:10:54,515 --> 00:10:56,395
He went in already.

159
00:11:00,271 --> 00:11:03,599
Escort these people downstairs
and tell the gate.

160
00:11:03,599 --> 00:11:07,887
If this happens one more time,
every one of them is getting fired.

161
00:11:07,887 --> 00:11:09,879
Yes, sir.

162
00:11:09,879 --> 00:11:11,859
Please come with me.

163
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:19,424
The view is incredible.

164
00:11:19,424 --> 00:11:22,283
It's so wide open. What a view.

165
00:11:22,283 --> 00:11:24,327
The wine's good, right?

166
00:11:24,327 --> 00:11:26,679
Huh? I've got some drinks.

167
00:11:26,679 --> 00:11:30,187
Not that cheap stuff. Drink something good.

168
00:11:30,187 --> 00:11:32,515
But you're unique and interesting.

169
00:11:32,515 --> 00:11:34,887
Honestly, you're not my type,

170
00:11:34,887 --> 00:11:36,926
but there's something kind of sexy about you.

171
00:11:39,859 --> 00:11:42,675
If you're here to play,
just play the darn game.

172
00:11:42,675 --> 00:11:44,815
Don't push your luck when you
haven't even been dealt a hand.

173
00:11:44,815 --> 00:11:46,943
Oh?

174
00:11:46,943 --> 00:11:49,492
I suddenly feel like
having something greasy, huh?

175
00:11:50,555 --> 00:11:53,926
I can order room service, right?

176
00:11:53,926 --> 00:11:56,310
Order whatever you want.

177
00:11:56,310 --> 00:11:58,159
And strong liquor...

178
00:11:59,123 --> 00:12:01,759
calls for greasy food.

179
00:12:05,663 --> 00:12:09,379
Tak Jong Gu just drugged the drink.
Just in case...

180
00:12:09,379 --> 00:12:11,843
No, it's too dangerous for you
to meet him there yourself.

181
00:12:11,843 --> 00:12:14,431
That woman could become a witness,
and we don't even have an escape route yet...

182
00:12:14,431 --> 00:12:15,943
Calm down, Ki Yeong Do.

183
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:18,479
Who's saying I'm meeting him right now?

184
00:12:18,479 --> 00:12:21,352
I'm just saying we need to prevent
anyone from getting hurt.

185
00:12:21,352 --> 00:12:22,963
Well...

186
00:12:22,963 --> 00:12:25,792
Maybe just a punch in the face or something?

187
00:12:38,815 --> 00:12:42,391
For their sake, I hope you won't do
anything reckless again.

188
00:12:42,391 --> 00:12:47,359
Of course. What have these people done wrong?
Someone else is guilty.

189
00:12:48,626 --> 00:12:51,392
Then please head back safely.

190
00:12:54,522 --> 00:12:57,392
That young man is almost annoyingly polite.

191
00:12:58,395 --> 00:13:03,492
Oh, we went all the way up there,
only to get kicked out empty-handed.

192
00:13:05,915 --> 00:13:07,947
Not empty-handed.

193
00:13:07,947 --> 00:13:09,703
- What?
- First.

194
00:13:09,703 --> 00:13:12,235
Chairman Cheon is
in the VIP gambling room now.

195
00:13:12,235 --> 00:13:14,487
Which means he was gambling.

196
00:13:14,487 --> 00:13:17,403
Chairman Cheon says
he has no appointments today.

197
00:13:17,403 --> 00:13:19,459
Oh, that's right.

198
00:13:19,459 --> 00:13:23,659
He didn't say there was no such person.
He said there was no appointment.

199
00:13:23,659 --> 00:13:26,451
Second, he's in his room right now.

200
00:13:26,451 --> 00:13:29,659
You're not seriously
going to his room, are you?

201
00:13:32,036 --> 00:13:35,359
Wait. Someone else is coming down the hall.

202
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,500
Come in.

203
00:13:46,091 --> 00:13:48,192
What did she order?

204
00:13:54,971 --> 00:13:56,671
Good!

205
00:14:10,819 --> 00:14:13,992
She said she was just washing her hands.
What's taking her so long?

206
00:14:28,899 --> 00:14:30,992
That worked fast, huh?

207
00:14:32,059 --> 00:14:34,083
♪ If you don't come out, I'm busting in ♪

208
00:14:34,083 --> 00:14:36,083
♪ Dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪

209
00:14:36,083 --> 00:14:38,259
♪ If you don't come out, I'm busting in ♪

210
00:14:42,215 --> 00:14:44,585
Oh, dear.

211
00:14:44,585 --> 00:14:48,907
Our Jong Gu, Jong Gu, Mr. Tak Jong Gu.

212
00:14:48,907 --> 00:14:51,835
You're not the only one who can use drugs.

213
00:14:51,835 --> 00:14:55,392
He probably never imagined
he'd be the one on the receiving end.

214
00:15:04,847 --> 00:15:06,331
Yeong Do, something's wrong.

215
00:15:06,331 --> 00:15:08,710
What is it? Is it the victim?

216
00:15:08,710 --> 00:15:11,339
No, I think Tak Jong Gu was drugged.

217
00:15:11,339 --> 00:15:12,860
What?

218
00:15:12,860 --> 00:15:14,592
What do you mean...

219
00:15:17,223 --> 00:15:19,834
So, should I tell the boss to start?

220
00:15:19,834 --> 00:15:23,279
Not yet. There's something
we need to check first.

221
00:15:23,279 --> 00:15:25,259
There's...

222
00:15:26,163 --> 00:15:27,863
someone in the bathroom.

223
00:15:51,351 --> 00:15:52,351
Who are you?

224
00:15:52,351 --> 00:15:54,876
That's not a kitchen knife.

225
00:15:54,876 --> 00:15:56,576
Are you a hitman?

226
00:16:15,431 --> 00:16:17,263
Yeah, this one's for people.

227
00:16:17,263 --> 00:16:18,535
We should at least
introduce ourselves, shouldn't we?

228
00:16:18,535 --> 00:16:19,891
- Do we have to?
- Ms. Yoo, what's going on?

229
00:16:19,891 --> 00:16:22,774
What's happening? Ms. Yoo!

230
00:16:24,087 --> 00:16:25,926
If you don't want to, we can skip it.

231
00:16:25,926 --> 00:16:28,592
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo!

232
00:16:38,534 --> 00:16:40,863
Stay calm. Take it slow.

233
00:16:40,863 --> 00:16:42,219
Did she sound like a professional?

234
00:16:42,219 --> 00:16:45,263
Judging by the fact that
she's going up against Ms. Bo Na,

235
00:16:45,263 --> 00:16:47,931
she doesn't seem like an ordinary person.

236
00:16:47,931 --> 00:16:51,013
I'll go check out the situation first.

237
00:16:51,013 --> 00:16:52,959
Ms. Yoo's in too much danger.

238
00:16:55,547 --> 00:16:59,626
This is all my fault. I missed my pass.

239
00:16:59,626 --> 00:17:01,327
Calm down.

240
00:17:01,327 --> 00:17:03,927
Director Yoo will be fine.

241
00:17:03,927 --> 00:17:05,334
This won't do.

242
00:17:05,334 --> 00:17:07,415
I'll take out all the CCTV cameras
in the building.

243
00:17:07,415 --> 00:17:11,592
Then the guards will all head
to the gaming room first.

244
00:17:22,298 --> 00:17:24,643
All the CCTV cameras just went down.

245
00:17:24,643 --> 00:17:27,031
Perfect timing. Let's start now.

246
00:17:27,031 --> 00:17:28,412
Stand by.

247
00:17:28,412 --> 00:17:30,492
Something just came up over here.

248
00:17:33,676 --> 00:17:36,026
What is taking so long?

249
00:17:39,327 --> 00:17:41,559
You lost?

250
00:18:02,191 --> 00:18:05,092
Looks like there aren't
any security guards here.

251
00:18:05,851 --> 00:18:07,983
That can't be.

252
00:18:07,983 --> 00:18:09,859
Could it be shift change?

253
00:18:50,487 --> 00:18:52,299
Huh?

254
00:18:52,299 --> 00:18:55,659
Didn't someone just walk past over there?

255
00:19:00,107 --> 00:19:01,526
What are you doing? Let go!

256
00:19:01,526 --> 00:19:04,259
Shh. Just be quiet for a second.

257
00:19:07,247 --> 00:19:10,067
Let's quickly find
Chairman Cheon's room first.

258
00:19:10,067 --> 00:19:11,939
Oh, alright.

259
00:19:11,939 --> 00:19:15,092
You said it was the best room
on the 24th floor, right?

260
00:19:16,095 --> 00:19:18,259
Darn it, let go of this!

261
00:19:32,019 --> 00:19:33,719
Shh!

262
00:19:52,287 --> 00:19:56,719
I'm in front of Tak Jong Gu's room.
It's quiet for now.

263
00:19:56,719 --> 00:19:58,526
But I'll go in.

264
00:20:18,359 --> 00:20:23,392
♪ In those four beats, there is love ♪

265
00:20:25,399 --> 00:20:27,259
There's a man too?

266
00:20:36,935 --> 00:20:40,192
He's just passed out from drinking.

267
00:20:41,027 --> 00:20:43,292
And who might you be?

268
00:20:48,767 --> 00:20:51,626
"Death conquers all evil."

269
00:20:51,626 --> 00:20:53,626
That's what our boss always says.

270
00:20:55,915 --> 00:20:59,363
So you guys are behind
what happened to my face?

271
00:20:59,363 --> 00:21:02,726
It's only temporary.
The symptoms will subside with time.

272
00:21:02,726 --> 00:21:05,592
You're the local team, aren't you?

273
00:21:07,835 --> 00:21:11,025
Well, things just got interesting.

274
00:21:11,025 --> 00:21:13,126
Are you guys Team A?

275
00:21:16,147 --> 00:21:18,607
It seems our clients have overlapped.

276
00:21:18,607 --> 00:21:20,826
That's never happened before.

277
00:21:22,075 --> 00:21:24,659
This should help ease the symptoms.

278
00:21:27,003 --> 00:21:29,427
But "overlap"?

279
00:21:29,427 --> 00:21:31,559
What do you mean?

280
00:21:32,371 --> 00:21:36,192
Isn't Tak Jong Gu your target?

281
00:21:39,531 --> 00:21:42,023
That punk was your target?

282
00:21:42,023 --> 00:21:44,299
No wonder.

283
00:21:44,299 --> 00:21:46,415
He wasn't ours.

284
00:21:46,415 --> 00:21:49,826
- Then...
- Our target is...

285
00:21:51,892 --> 00:21:54,326
Room 2408.

286
00:21:55,235 --> 00:21:57,026
- ♪ Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪
- Gaecheon Construction,

287
00:21:57,026 --> 00:22:01,023
- ♪ In those four beats ♪
- Chairman Cheon Seong Gil.

288
00:22:01,023 --> 00:22:05,959
♪ There is love, and there are tears ♪

289
00:22:12,095 --> 00:22:14,026
2408.

290
00:22:18,127 --> 00:22:20,726
Well, what a stroke of luck, huh?

291
00:22:20,726 --> 00:22:23,059
You've just made my job easier.

292
00:22:24,075 --> 00:22:27,084
Hey, you, just leave.

293
00:22:27,084 --> 00:22:31,092
I'm letting you live as a special favor
for bringing me here.

294
00:22:32,395 --> 00:22:34,863
- What are you doing?
- Jeez.

295
00:22:34,863 --> 00:22:38,792
That's none of your business,
so leave while I'm letting you walk out.

296
00:22:38,792 --> 00:22:40,327
You don't exactly look

297
00:22:40,327 --> 00:22:43,992
innocent enough to go around
calling yourself a witness,

298
00:22:43,992 --> 00:22:46,587
so I'm letting you go.

299
00:22:46,587 --> 00:22:48,975
I only want to kill one person today.

300
00:22:48,975 --> 00:22:50,675
- Hey!
- Darn it!

301
00:22:55,407 --> 00:22:58,711
Ms. Yoo, can you hear me? Ms. Yoo?

302
00:22:58,711 --> 00:23:00,843
Please, say something! Please!

303
00:23:00,843 --> 00:23:01,987
Ms. Yoo!

304
00:23:01,987 --> 00:23:05,392
I need to know why you're trying to kill him.

305
00:23:09,667 --> 00:23:11,131
I gave you a fair chance.

306
00:23:11,131 --> 00:23:12,515
I gave you one too.

307
00:23:12,515 --> 00:23:13,780
Are you a hired killer?

308
00:23:13,780 --> 00:23:15,463
She is with the local team.

309
00:23:15,463 --> 00:23:16,819
Are you listening?

310
00:23:16,819 --> 00:23:19,726
Ms. Yoo, you have to stop, please!

311
00:23:23,579 --> 00:23:25,559
I'm not holding back anymore.

312
00:23:25,559 --> 00:23:26,559
Fine. Go ahead.

313
00:23:26,559 --> 00:23:28,092
Ms. Yoo!

314
00:23:28,092 --> 00:23:30,092
Ms. Yoo, please...

315
00:23:39,707 --> 00:23:43,339
♪ Dun-da, Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪

316
00:23:43,339 --> 00:23:47,059
♪ In those four beats ♪

317
00:23:47,059 --> 00:23:50,792
♪ There is love, and there are tears ♪

318
00:23:50,792 --> 00:23:54,727
♪ And there is farewell too ♪

319
00:23:54,727 --> 00:23:57,319
♪ With each verse, each hurdle ♪

320
00:23:57,319 --> 00:24:00,292
♪ When you overcome it ♪

321
00:24:11,811 --> 00:24:14,095
I think this is it, right?

322
00:24:14,095 --> 00:24:17,659
But don't you hear something inside?

323
00:24:43,811 --> 00:24:46,083
Sounds like some guys
horsing around in there.

324
00:24:46,083 --> 00:24:48,359
Isn't this the place?

325
00:24:51,075 --> 00:24:53,307
What's going on?

326
00:24:53,307 --> 00:24:56,035
Do you need any help?

327
00:24:56,035 --> 00:24:57,735
No.

328
00:25:00,026 --> 00:25:02,283
I must've gotten the room wrong.

329
00:25:02,283 --> 00:25:03,947
I told you it wasn't this room, didn't I?

330
00:25:03,947 --> 00:25:05,958
See? I told you I was right.

331
00:25:05,958 --> 00:25:08,051
- It's upstairs.
- I said it's the floor above.

332
00:25:08,051 --> 00:25:11,015
I've been telling you this whole time.
It's the floor above.

333
00:25:11,015 --> 00:25:13,512
But this is the top floor, though.

334
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:17,563
Suspicious people are lurking in front of
room 2408, so go check it out.

335
00:25:17,563 --> 00:25:19,759
Yeah, I'm going right now.

336
00:25:21,111 --> 00:25:23,995
Wow, we almost got caught.

337
00:25:23,995 --> 00:25:27,291
I thought my heart was going to explode.

338
00:25:27,291 --> 00:25:29,243
I think she's gone.

339
00:25:29,243 --> 00:25:31,895
I'm too scared to keep going.

340
00:25:31,895 --> 00:25:34,059
Can't we just pull out for today?

341
00:25:34,059 --> 00:25:36,243
Come on, what have you even done? Get up.

342
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:39,792
Even if we're pulling out,
we should at least ring the doorbell first.

343
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:47,326
Wait, hold up!

344
00:25:49,299 --> 00:25:51,111
Please don't misunderstand
the current situation.

345
00:25:51,111 --> 00:25:52,326
The employees downstairs

346
00:25:52,326 --> 00:25:54,159
- are completely innocent.
- Shh!

347
00:25:56,571 --> 00:25:59,795
Don't do anything else.
Just go straight down to the first floor.

348
00:25:59,795 --> 00:26:03,126
If you leave the building now,
I'll pretend I never saw you.

349
00:26:09,159 --> 00:26:10,859
What was that?

350
00:26:13,087 --> 00:26:14,673
Darn it!

351
00:26:14,673 --> 00:26:16,526
Seriously...

352
00:26:19,226 --> 00:26:23,647
You're good at scurrying away like a rat.

353
00:26:23,647 --> 00:26:27,041
How long are you going to keep blocking me?

354
00:26:27,041 --> 00:26:31,192
Oh... Is blocking all you can do?

355
00:26:31,899 --> 00:26:33,173
Curious?

356
00:26:33,173 --> 00:26:34,873
You!

357
00:26:45,779 --> 00:26:48,126
Then try blocking me yourself.

358
00:27:04,515 --> 00:27:08,026
What are you? What kind of woman are you?

359
00:27:09,971 --> 00:27:11,826
The water stopped.

360
00:27:18,526 --> 00:27:21,426
Director Yoo Bo Na, it's me!

361
00:27:22,187 --> 00:27:23,887
You...

362
00:27:30,311 --> 00:27:34,519
♪ Dun-da, Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪

363
00:27:34,519 --> 00:27:38,059
♪ In those four beats ♪

364
00:27:44,947 --> 00:27:46,943
Oh, yeah, Secretary Kim.

365
00:27:46,943 --> 00:27:50,343
After that soak, I'm getting a little hungry.

366
00:27:50,343 --> 00:27:53,226
Shall I grab a bite before heading down?

367
00:27:53,878 --> 00:27:56,207
Alright, alright.

368
00:27:56,207 --> 00:28:01,083
♪ There is love, and there is farewell ♪

369
00:28:01,083 --> 00:28:04,926
♪ And there are tears too ♪

370
00:28:08,092 --> 00:28:11,792
What a spectacular day this has been.

371
00:28:11,792 --> 00:28:13,879
How are your nerves holding up?

372
00:28:13,879 --> 00:28:16,467
You're scared out of your wits.

373
00:28:16,467 --> 00:28:20,359
I didn't know meeting one person
could be this hard.

374
00:28:25,247 --> 00:28:27,859
It's like a giant fortress.

375
00:28:28,719 --> 00:28:31,192
Like a solid castle wall.

376
00:28:31,192 --> 00:28:32,759
It does.

377
00:28:32,759 --> 00:28:36,548
In movies, places that look this glamorous

378
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:40,092
usually have some dark secret
lurking underneath.

379
00:28:40,855 --> 00:28:44,559
Eventually, those secrets
always come to light.

380
00:28:45,626 --> 00:28:48,592
That's what people like us are here for.

381
00:28:51,759 --> 00:28:52,759
Nice to meet you.

382
00:28:52,759 --> 00:28:55,115
I'm Bae Bi Ji, owner of Dalsam Auto.

383
00:28:55,115 --> 00:28:59,811
Hello. I'm Go Yeong Gap, Manager of
Sales Team 3 at Durumi Electronics.

384
00:28:59,811 --> 00:29:04,735
Oh, and this is our team hacker,
Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do.

385
00:29:04,735 --> 00:29:07,026
A hacker?

386
00:29:07,026 --> 00:29:10,520
So the CCTV going down was his doing.

387
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:14,611
I've heard there are separate teams
for different regions and assignments,

388
00:29:14,611 --> 00:29:16,211
but this is my first time
meeting you in person.

389
00:29:16,211 --> 00:29:17,619
Well, unless something unexpected
like this happens,

390
00:29:17,619 --> 00:29:19,792
we don't really cross paths.

391
00:29:20,767 --> 00:29:21,923
Oh, and this is...

392
00:29:21,923 --> 00:29:24,433
Oh, no need to introduce her.
I know her well.

393
00:29:24,433 --> 00:29:28,292
Is there anyone in this line of work
who doesn't know Director Yoo?

394
00:29:28,959 --> 00:29:30,943
I've met her before too.

395
00:29:30,943 --> 00:29:32,792
Back when Ms. Bae was team leader.

396
00:29:33,661 --> 00:29:34,995
Yeah.

397
00:29:34,995 --> 00:29:37,992
You were just a rookie back then.
You're a team leader already?

398
00:29:38,651 --> 00:29:42,192
Well, it wasn't exactly intentional.
There's a bit of a story behind it.

399
00:29:42,847 --> 00:29:44,583
Oh, these are our employees.

400
00:29:44,583 --> 00:29:46,971
This is Ms. Mun Meo Ru,
who mainly works in the field.

401
00:29:46,971 --> 00:29:50,775
Wow, it's a miracle she survived
going up against you, Director Yoo.

402
00:29:50,775 --> 00:29:52,785
Didn't you go a little easy on her?

403
00:29:52,785 --> 00:29:54,057
What? She was pretty good.

404
00:29:54,057 --> 00:29:57,211
Though she does seem a little reckless.

405
00:29:57,211 --> 00:30:01,492
Yes, well, thank you for sparing me.

406
00:30:05,139 --> 00:30:09,791
And this is our team's idea machine,
our part-timer, Ms. Mun Da Rae.

407
00:30:09,791 --> 00:30:12,507
Oh, it's cold.

408
00:30:12,507 --> 00:30:16,059
She seems to have the most experience,
but her position is still just part-time.

409
00:30:16,059 --> 00:30:19,467
She really hates being
responsible for anything.

410
00:30:19,467 --> 00:30:20,855
You know me, right?

411
00:30:20,855 --> 00:30:22,320
We met at the casino earlier.

412
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:25,359
I know you, chicken heart.

413
00:30:26,398 --> 00:30:28,099
But how did you pull that off?

414
00:30:28,099 --> 00:30:31,855
You had a higher win rate
than the program I designed.

415
00:30:31,855 --> 00:30:34,123
Use your brain, your brain.

416
00:30:34,123 --> 00:30:38,274
You stupidly cling to machines,
so you get outsmarted that stupidly.

417
00:30:38,274 --> 00:30:40,259
Oh, dear, I'm sorry.

418
00:30:41,395 --> 00:30:45,159
Our part-timer is brilliant,
but she's a little lacking in social skills.

419
00:30:47,895 --> 00:30:50,600
Then shall we hear about your client?

420
00:30:50,600 --> 00:30:53,726
Oh, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil?

421
00:30:54,399 --> 00:30:57,019
In a nutshell, he's a serial sexual predator.

422
00:30:57,019 --> 00:30:58,923
He was caught red-handed a few years ago,

423
00:30:58,923 --> 00:31:01,347
but got away with a suspended sentence.

424
00:31:01,347 --> 00:31:05,727
He hired the wife of one of his
construction workers as a housekeeper,

425
00:31:05,727 --> 00:31:09,415
and repeatedly sexually assaulted her
by threatening her husband's job.

426
00:31:09,415 --> 00:31:10,883
Her husband found out

427
00:31:10,883 --> 00:31:14,759
and threatened to go to the press
unless he confessed.

428
00:31:14,759 --> 00:31:18,711
So, Chairman Cheon bribed
a fellow worker with a criminal record

429
00:31:18,711 --> 00:31:20,571
and had him murder the husband.

430
00:31:20,571 --> 00:31:22,339
Then he covered it up by staging the murder

431
00:31:22,339 --> 00:31:25,987
as an accidental fall caused by
the victim's own negligence.

432
00:31:25,987 --> 00:31:28,559
Help me! Please!

433
00:31:28,559 --> 00:31:31,770
Save me! I was wrong.
I said I was wrong. Please save me.

434
00:31:31,770 --> 00:31:34,215
We just met with the coworker

435
00:31:34,215 --> 00:31:36,592
who was hired
to kill the husband a few days ago.

436
00:31:38,419 --> 00:31:43,592
Chairman Cheon must be thrilled that
the guy who had dirt on him is dead.

437
00:31:45,459 --> 00:31:46,459
Oh, right!

438
00:31:46,459 --> 00:31:50,614
I think two reporters were following
Chairman Cheon earlier.

439
00:31:50,614 --> 00:31:51,728
Reporters?

440
00:31:51,728 --> 00:31:54,147
The media lost interest quickly

441
00:31:54,147 --> 00:31:56,243
because Chairman Cheon
cleverly covered up the case.

442
00:31:56,243 --> 00:32:00,723
So I thought it was interesting that
reporters are still digging into it.

443
00:32:00,723 --> 00:32:02,992
They seemed pretty persistent.

444
00:32:02,992 --> 00:32:07,019
I sent them away because it seemed dangerous
if they kept getting closer,

445
00:32:07,019 --> 00:32:08,892
but I'm not sure if they've actually left.

446
00:32:12,959 --> 00:32:14,792
Yul, I'll close the door. Watch your hand.

447
00:32:16,495 --> 00:32:19,111
But, honey, are you
really sure you have time?

448
00:32:19,111 --> 00:32:22,155
If you think it might be tough,
should we quickly ask Se Ah now?

449
00:32:22,155 --> 00:32:25,819
I do have an interview
a little farther away...

450
00:32:25,819 --> 00:32:27,295
But I should be fine. I can make it on time.

451
00:32:27,295 --> 00:32:29,735
Bad guys don't usually give you much time.

452
00:32:29,735 --> 00:32:31,215
Yeah? A bad guy?

453
00:32:31,215 --> 00:32:33,192
How bad is this guy?

454
00:32:34,278 --> 00:32:38,726
On the surface, it looks like an accident,
but a premeditated murder underneath?

455
00:32:38,726 --> 00:32:42,292
I'm going to expose the person
who ordered it and make sure he pays.

456
00:32:48,027 --> 00:32:50,175
So why did you go after Tak Jong Gu?

457
00:32:50,175 --> 00:32:54,027
We were looking for a fool
who could get us onto the VIP floor.

458
00:32:54,027 --> 00:32:57,920
We planned to set that room on fire
and sneak into Cheon Seong Gil's room

459
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:59,926
during the chaos for the meeting.

460
00:33:00,635 --> 00:33:02,492
You came up with
quite a complicated scenario.

461
00:33:02,492 --> 00:33:07,800
Coming all the way to a casino,
and even playing games yourself to do it?

462
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:12,159
She just made it fit
because she wanted to gamble.

463
00:33:14,567 --> 00:33:17,171
Anyway, they weren't even
particularly difficult meetings,

464
00:33:17,171 --> 00:33:19,503
but since our dates and routes overlapped,

465
00:33:19,503 --> 00:33:22,259
we ended up unintentionally
interfering with each other.

466
00:33:24,459 --> 00:33:29,359
Since we're already in this together,
how about we work together this time?

467
00:33:30,799 --> 00:33:33,126
Well, sounds like a good idea.

468
00:33:33,126 --> 00:33:36,826
- I'm in.
- If Ms. Yoo is okay with it, I'm fine too.

469
00:33:37,839 --> 00:33:43,827
We've never worked together before,
so we don't know each other's styles.

470
00:33:43,827 --> 00:33:45,499
Isn't this a bit of a gamble?

471
00:33:45,499 --> 00:33:47,983
Oh, I like a gamble.

472
00:33:47,983 --> 00:33:49,639
- I'm in!
- I'm against it.

473
00:33:49,639 --> 00:33:51,043
I'm not feeling great.

474
00:33:51,043 --> 00:33:52,987
Well, looks like the vote went in favor.

475
00:33:52,987 --> 00:33:54,411
Let's do the collaboration.

476
00:33:54,411 --> 00:33:57,659
Jeez, she always does whatever she wants.

477
00:34:00,426 --> 00:34:02,467
Yeah, we should.

478
00:34:02,467 --> 00:34:05,526
Our part-timer is a bit of a dictator.

479
00:34:07,147 --> 00:34:09,611
But we have to wrap up the meeting
by tomorrow.

480
00:34:09,611 --> 00:34:12,503
Do we have time to rework the scenario?

481
00:34:12,503 --> 00:34:13,692
Why drag it out till tomorrow?

482
00:34:13,692 --> 00:34:16,059
We've already got the whole story.

483
00:34:16,059 --> 00:34:18,511
For this one...

484
00:34:18,511 --> 00:34:20,604
let's go with Go-Stop.

485
00:34:20,604 --> 00:34:24,259
Kill two birds with one stone.

486
00:34:24,259 --> 00:34:28,219
Isn't it risky to meet Tak Jong Gu again?

487
00:34:28,219 --> 00:34:30,026
If he finds out we drugged him...

488
00:34:31,499 --> 00:34:32,791
All mine!

489
00:34:32,791 --> 00:34:34,339
He's a junkie.

490
00:34:34,339 --> 00:34:35,931
He'll think the wine was switched by mistake

491
00:34:35,931 --> 00:34:38,143
and that he drank his own drugged wine.

492
00:34:38,143 --> 00:34:39,270
What?

493
00:34:39,270 --> 00:34:40,643
I thought you'd left. You're still here?

494
00:34:40,643 --> 00:34:42,594
I got a room too.

495
00:34:42,594 --> 00:34:44,559
Are you sober now?

496
00:34:44,559 --> 00:34:45,967
Yeah.

497
00:34:45,967 --> 00:34:51,959
Well, I'm usually a heavy drinker,
but one lousy drink knocked me out.

498
00:34:52,663 --> 00:34:55,226
Anyway, good to see you again.

499
00:34:55,226 --> 00:34:57,626
Oh, this is boring.

500
00:34:57,626 --> 00:34:59,719
Why is there no thrill in this?

501
00:34:59,719 --> 00:35:02,792
I'm not feeling any dopamine.

502
00:35:04,355 --> 00:35:06,747
Want to come back to my room?

503
00:35:06,747 --> 00:35:09,291
I've got something seriously killer.

504
00:35:09,291 --> 00:35:14,135
You pathetic junkie prick who thinks
your rich dad makes you untouchable.

505
00:35:14,135 --> 00:35:15,135
What?

506
00:35:15,135 --> 00:35:17,567
Someone said that about you.

507
00:35:17,567 --> 00:35:18,767
Is that true?

508
00:35:18,767 --> 00:35:20,579
Who said that?

509
00:35:20,579 --> 00:35:23,263
Which punk talked nonsense like that?

510
00:35:23,263 --> 00:35:25,484
Over there...

511
00:35:25,484 --> 00:35:27,659
some old guy with a big belly.

512
00:35:28,783 --> 00:35:30,671
Your name is Tak Jong Gu, right?

513
00:35:30,671 --> 00:35:32,563
I heard he's some chairman.

514
00:35:32,563 --> 00:35:35,931
Oh, Gaecheon Construction?

515
00:35:35,931 --> 00:35:37,503
Gaecheon?

516
00:35:37,503 --> 00:35:39,315
Has the old man lost his mind?

517
00:35:39,315 --> 00:35:41,059
Give me a good hand.

518
00:35:44,419 --> 00:35:46,612
Oh, my, what is this?

519
00:35:46,612 --> 00:35:49,659
- Old man, have you lost your mind?
- Oh, my, what's this?

520
00:35:49,659 --> 00:35:53,311
You little punk who keeps paying off
my old man every quarter.

521
00:35:53,311 --> 00:35:55,381
You think you're untouchable, huh?

522
00:35:55,381 --> 00:35:56,692
Hey, what are you? Hey!

523
00:35:56,692 --> 00:35:58,891
- What on earth are you...
- Watch your mouth, or else, huh?

524
00:35:58,891 --> 00:36:01,311
Maybe you'll come to your senses
when your company goes under.

525
00:36:01,311 --> 00:36:02,719
Darn it!

526
00:36:02,719 --> 00:36:04,419
Hey!

527
00:36:06,595 --> 00:36:10,807
- What are you?
- That should be enough witnesses.

528
00:36:10,807 --> 00:36:13,619
- What's next?
- Wow...

529
00:36:13,619 --> 00:36:17,359
I really like that
you're a total punk, Jong Gu.

530
00:36:19,827 --> 00:36:22,292
That killer stuff you mentioned earlier...

531
00:36:23,051 --> 00:36:24,792
is that offer still good?

532
00:36:27,903 --> 00:36:29,603
Are you interested in that?

533
00:36:30,219 --> 00:36:31,959
Of course, it is.

534
00:36:33,047 --> 00:36:35,892
One dose, and you're off to heaven.

535
00:36:38,495 --> 00:36:40,823
Bring that to my room in an hour.

536
00:36:40,823 --> 00:36:43,392
Without anyone knowing.

537
00:36:48,911 --> 00:36:54,615
When Tak Jong Gu walks into the room
and finds Chairman Cheon dead,

538
00:36:54,615 --> 00:36:56,926
he'll be shocked into passing out.

539
00:36:56,926 --> 00:37:02,279
Yeah, we'll give the unconscious guy
the drug we brought first.

540
00:37:02,279 --> 00:37:06,675
Then Team A can go in
and finish off Tak Jong Gu.

541
00:37:06,675 --> 00:37:08,035
Bingo!

542
00:37:08,035 --> 00:37:12,705
Tak Jong Gu, still furious even after
causing that scene in the gaming room,

543
00:37:12,705 --> 00:37:15,395
takes a full dose of drugs, loses his mind,

544
00:37:15,395 --> 00:37:17,583
and storms into Cheon Seong Gil's room.

545
00:37:17,583 --> 00:37:19,492
We'll take him out first.

546
00:37:19,492 --> 00:37:24,719
Then he'll throw himself
out the window. Boom!

547
00:37:24,719 --> 00:37:26,419
Done.

548
00:37:37,692 --> 00:37:39,892
[Big Precious]

549
00:37:42,359 --> 00:37:45,192
Honey, I'm on my way to pick up Yul.
I'm almost there.

550
00:37:45,192 --> 00:37:46,890
Are you going to Seo Yeon's place now?

551
00:37:46,890 --> 00:37:48,563
I'm sorry, I'm a bit late, right?

552
00:37:48,563 --> 00:37:51,651
But I called ahead to let them know.

553
00:37:51,651 --> 00:37:53,549
No, I'm not nagging you.

554
00:37:53,549 --> 00:37:55,223
Have you eaten?

555
00:37:55,223 --> 00:37:58,399
I can just eat at home later.
What about you, honey?

556
00:37:58,399 --> 00:38:01,031
Well, I grabbed something quick.

557
00:38:01,031 --> 00:38:03,835
I'm still out. I haven't finished work yet.

558
00:38:03,835 --> 00:38:05,351
Still?

559
00:38:05,351 --> 00:38:08,547
Didn't you have a client meeting today?
Did it not go well?

560
00:38:08,547 --> 00:38:13,159
Oh, the meeting fell through this afternoon,
so it got pushed to tonight.

561
00:38:14,099 --> 00:38:16,963
Did the interview with the bad guy go well?

562
00:38:16,963 --> 00:38:18,623
Me? Well...

563
00:38:18,623 --> 00:38:20,747
It's not like I had an appointment with him.

564
00:38:20,747 --> 00:38:25,143
And bad guys don't usually
give interviews willingly, you know.

565
00:38:25,143 --> 00:38:26,143
Then what do I do?

566
00:38:26,143 --> 00:38:27,811
I just have to barge in.

567
00:38:27,811 --> 00:38:29,435
So, did you meet him?

568
00:38:29,435 --> 00:38:33,527
I did meet him,
but I got kicked out right away.

569
00:38:33,527 --> 00:38:35,791
I couldn't even ask one question.

570
00:38:35,791 --> 00:38:37,527
Oh, I see.

571
00:38:37,527 --> 00:38:40,727
It's okay. I'll just barge in again tomorrow.

572
00:38:40,727 --> 00:38:42,387
Honey, I'm almost there.

573
00:38:42,387 --> 00:38:43,759
Can we talk again later?

574
00:38:43,759 --> 00:38:44,792
Yul's probably waiting.

575
00:38:44,792 --> 00:38:45,892
Yeah, okay.

576
00:38:45,892 --> 00:38:47,467
Make sure you eat.

577
00:38:47,467 --> 00:38:49,167
Okay.

578
00:39:01,403 --> 00:39:05,192
Tak Jong Gu's actions are not deviating
from expectations one bit.

579
00:39:05,192 --> 00:39:08,259
Everything went according to plan
up to the gaming room.

580
00:39:08,955 --> 00:39:10,655
Yeah.

581
00:39:12,031 --> 00:39:14,351
You've seemed a little off, Ms. Yoo.

582
00:39:14,351 --> 00:39:17,059
Is something bothering you?

583
00:39:20,032 --> 00:39:22,673
I saw my husband at the casino earlier.

584
00:39:22,673 --> 00:39:24,373
Your husband?

585
00:39:26,623 --> 00:39:29,759
Then that man I saw earlier was...

586
00:39:29,759 --> 00:39:31,607
I'll find out where he is right now.

587
00:39:31,607 --> 00:39:33,153
I just talked to him on the phone.

588
00:39:33,153 --> 00:39:34,707
He said he's on his way home.

589
00:39:34,707 --> 00:39:37,059
We won't run into each other anymore.

590
00:39:38,591 --> 00:39:41,992
But your husband being here...

591
00:39:43,239 --> 00:39:45,192
Could it be that gambling...

592
00:39:46,307 --> 00:39:48,092
That can't be right.

593
00:39:48,883 --> 00:39:50,691
Sorry.

594
00:39:50,691 --> 00:39:54,019
He said he had an interview
out of town today.

595
00:39:54,019 --> 00:39:56,355
But I didn't expect him to be here.

596
00:39:56,355 --> 00:39:58,792
An interview, with whom?

597
00:39:58,792 --> 00:40:02,459
Oh, the reporter who's digging into
Chairman Cheon...

598
00:40:05,279 --> 00:40:06,855
Let's get to work.

599
00:40:06,855 --> 00:40:09,652
Where are the two of them now?

600
00:40:09,652 --> 00:40:13,827
Okay, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
just went into his room,

601
00:40:13,827 --> 00:40:16,947
and Tak Jong Gu went into his room too.

602
00:40:16,947 --> 00:40:18,875
Then the timing should work.

603
00:40:18,875 --> 00:40:21,092
Okay, shall we go?

604
00:40:22,651 --> 00:40:24,351
Ms. Yoo.

605
00:40:25,807 --> 00:40:28,099
Never leave me out again.

606
00:40:28,099 --> 00:40:30,711
That won't happen again, okay?

607
00:40:30,711 --> 00:40:32,411
I'm going.

608
00:41:00,307 --> 00:41:01,767
Wow!

609
00:41:01,767 --> 00:41:03,467
Nice room!

610
00:41:06,947 --> 00:41:10,441
My baby, where are you?

611
00:41:10,441 --> 00:41:12,851
Are you getting ready for something special?

612
00:41:12,851 --> 00:41:15,126
I love the outfit you had on earlier.

613
00:41:25,767 --> 00:41:29,275
That darn punk made me shower again.

614
00:41:29,275 --> 00:41:31,723
I'm so annoyed.

615
00:41:31,723 --> 00:41:34,192
Oh, my, so annoying.

616
00:41:35,831 --> 00:41:37,487
What? Who are you?

617
00:41:37,487 --> 00:41:39,726
Who are you? Huh?

618
00:41:43,039 --> 00:41:46,191
You little punk, you...

619
00:41:46,191 --> 00:41:48,835
Why on earth are you here?

620
00:41:48,835 --> 00:41:50,919
What are you doing in my woman's room?

621
00:41:50,919 --> 00:41:54,559
Jeez, you punk, you're in for it now.

622
00:41:54,559 --> 00:41:58,967
Get over here! You punk!

623
00:41:58,967 --> 00:42:00,459
Punk?

624
00:42:00,459 --> 00:42:02,892
Should I tear you apart?

625
00:42:15,551 --> 00:42:16,939
You two make quite a pair.

626
00:42:16,939 --> 00:42:19,559
I think there's a simpler way,
don't you think?

627
00:42:19,559 --> 00:42:24,895
I saw a small light outside
Chairman Cheon's room window.

628
00:42:24,895 --> 00:42:29,255
You're good at scurrying away like a rat.

629
00:42:29,255 --> 00:42:31,626
How long are you going to keep blocking me?

630
00:42:32,726 --> 00:42:35,026
If I'm right...

631
00:42:38,879 --> 00:42:40,579
You're right.

632
00:42:41,792 --> 00:42:45,643
Cheon Seong Gil's room and Tak Jong Gu's room
are on the opposite rear line.

633
00:42:45,643 --> 00:42:47,759
Outside those windows,
there are two mountains on either end,

634
00:42:47,759 --> 00:42:52,027
and a cable car is running
back and forth between them.

635
00:42:52,027 --> 00:42:53,727
Then...

636
00:42:55,727 --> 00:42:59,683
As things stand, everyone here
could be called in by the police

637
00:42:59,683 --> 00:43:01,427
during the investigation.

638
00:43:01,427 --> 00:43:06,635
Especially those who had direct contact
with Cheon Seong Gil and Tak Jong Gu.

639
00:43:06,635 --> 00:43:08,331
There'll be plenty of witnesses.

640
00:43:08,331 --> 00:43:11,335
Let's just take the long way
and kill two birds with one stone, yeah?

641
00:43:11,335 --> 00:43:13,035
You're right.

642
00:43:17,926 --> 00:43:19,007
Hey, you punk!

643
00:43:19,007 --> 00:43:22,179
How dare some young punk
talk to an adult like that?

644
00:43:22,179 --> 00:43:25,995
Darn it! Hey! You want me
to chop your hand off?

645
00:43:25,995 --> 00:43:28,263
You ungrateful punk!

646
00:43:28,263 --> 00:43:29,791
I've been letting you get away with it,
but now you've gone too far!

647
00:43:29,791 --> 00:43:32,939
- Give it to me!
- Hand it over!

648
00:43:32,939 --> 00:43:35,415
I'll make you go through exactly
what I went through.

649
00:43:35,415 --> 00:43:36,719
Why won't this open?

650
00:43:36,719 --> 00:43:40,643
Hey, that's expensive, okay?

651
00:43:40,643 --> 00:43:41,892
Give that up, you old geezer!

652
00:43:41,892 --> 00:43:43,559
What?

653
00:43:43,559 --> 00:43:45,687
What? You little...

654
00:43:45,687 --> 00:43:48,067
What? Old geezer?

655
00:43:48,067 --> 00:43:50,351
Darn it!

656
00:43:50,351 --> 00:43:52,591
Old geezer! Old geezer!

657
00:43:52,591 --> 00:43:54,492
Okay, shall we go?

658
00:44:29,671 --> 00:44:31,659
Give it back! It's mine!

659
00:44:58,011 --> 00:45:00,826
One-two, client meeting completed.

660
00:45:17,147 --> 00:45:20,047
Alright, good work, everyone.

661
00:45:20,047 --> 00:45:23,027
Get some good rest tomorrow,
and I'll see you all the day after.

662
00:45:23,027 --> 00:45:24,727
Yeah.

663
00:45:29,959 --> 00:45:34,235
I wish I'd gotten to see
that historic moment with my own eyes.

664
00:45:34,235 --> 00:45:35,792
At least we saved the cost of a bullet.

665
00:45:35,792 --> 00:45:38,647
Our operating expenses were already tight.

666
00:45:38,647 --> 00:45:43,695
But I never knew there were people
in the area doing the same thing.

667
00:45:43,695 --> 00:45:48,492
There are too many bad guys in the world
for us to handle them all ourselves.

668
00:45:52,527 --> 00:45:54,492
Rest in peace, everyone.

669
00:45:55,647 --> 00:45:57,826
You two are headed the same way,

670
00:45:58,899 --> 00:46:01,059
so at least you won't be bored.

671
00:46:06,910 --> 00:46:09,959
Is our Tae Soon thirsty?

672
00:46:09,959 --> 00:46:14,263
Oh, alright. I'll give you some more water.

673
00:46:14,263 --> 00:46:18,591
Drink plenty of water,
and let's live together for a long time.

674
00:46:18,591 --> 00:46:22,092
I'll even get you another supplement
for your birthday this year.

675
00:46:24,937 --> 00:46:27,792
Looks like someone made Yoo Bo Na mad.

676
00:46:28,811 --> 00:46:31,892
No, it's nothing. Not you.
I mean, your owner.

677
00:46:31,892 --> 00:46:35,092
Yeah, want some more water?

678
00:46:35,092 --> 00:46:36,792
Yeah.

679
00:46:39,699 --> 00:46:41,892
Oh, my, so pretty!

680
00:46:41,892 --> 00:46:44,592
Alright, alright.

681
00:46:48,515 --> 00:46:51,011
Wow, as expected of Kingfisher.

682
00:46:51,011 --> 00:46:55,392
I finally got to meet the legend I've only
heard about. Today is my lucky day.

683
00:46:56,042 --> 00:46:57,042
You happy?

684
00:46:57,042 --> 00:47:00,791
What's so exciting about
getting carried by someone else?

685
00:47:00,791 --> 00:47:04,292
At least we won't
be getting called in by the police.

686
00:47:04,292 --> 00:47:07,292
There's no more perfect alibi than this.

687
00:47:08,279 --> 00:47:11,811
Hey, we're done for the day,
so let's go get some drinks.

688
00:47:11,811 --> 00:47:14,992
A day like this calls for chicken and beer.

689
00:47:16,423 --> 00:47:18,675
It's on me today.

690
00:47:18,675 --> 00:47:21,359
Ah, on me, on me!

691
00:47:22,131 --> 00:47:24,191
She looks the happiest of all.

692
00:47:24,191 --> 00:47:26,499
No, she's scared right now.

693
00:47:26,499 --> 00:47:30,247
She's just pretending to be tough.

694
00:47:30,247 --> 00:47:31,859
Hey, why don't you quit gambling
while you're at it?

695
00:47:31,859 --> 00:47:36,887
Hurry up! Whoever's late has to
write their name with their butt!

696
00:47:36,887 --> 00:47:39,626
Da Rae, I'll just be late!

697
00:47:40,423 --> 00:47:41,815
Oh, how embarrassing.

698
00:47:41,815 --> 00:47:45,771
Oh, this is so humiliating. Oh, I hate this.

699
00:47:45,771 --> 00:47:47,859
Oh, being the boss is really hard.

700
00:47:47,859 --> 00:47:49,692
What's wrong with him?

701
00:47:52,927 --> 00:47:54,375
Daddy, why isn't Mommy here?

702
00:47:54,375 --> 00:47:57,145
I told you Mommy was staying the night.

703
00:47:57,145 --> 00:48:00,659
If Yul goes to sleep
and goes to daycare tomorrow,

704
00:48:00,659 --> 00:48:03,351
Mommy will be there to greet you with, "Yul!"

705
00:48:03,351 --> 00:48:05,303
But where did Mommy go?

706
00:48:05,303 --> 00:48:07,179
She went to work.

707
00:48:07,179 --> 00:48:08,923
Hmm... Something important?

708
00:48:08,923 --> 00:48:11,892
Huh? What kind of work?

709
00:48:13,366 --> 00:48:16,647
Wait, wait.

710
00:48:16,647 --> 00:48:19,392
Sit down here for a minute. Have a seat.

711
00:48:22,094 --> 00:48:24,287
Oh, Ms. Gu, did you get home okay?

712
00:48:24,287 --> 00:48:25,287
What made you call this late?

713
00:48:25,287 --> 00:48:29,039
Mr. Kwon, did you see the breaking news?

714
00:48:29,039 --> 00:48:30,579
Breaking news?

715
00:48:30,579 --> 00:48:32,879
What is it? But what's wrong with your voice?

716
00:48:32,879 --> 00:48:37,135
Chairman Cheon Seong Gil... is dead.
He was shot by Kingfisher.

717
00:48:37,135 --> 00:48:38,927
What?

718
00:48:38,927 --> 00:48:41,539
Two guests were shot and killed

719
00:48:41,539 --> 00:48:45,399
by a sniper in a VIP suite
at a casino hotel this evening.

720
00:48:45,399 --> 00:48:50,243
Police are leaning toward Kingfisher
being behind this attack as well.

721
00:48:50,243 --> 00:48:51,731
[Kingfisher Strikes Again]
This is the first time

722
00:48:51,731 --> 00:48:54,430
[Two Casino VIP Guests Killed]
two people have been killed

723
00:48:54,430 --> 00:48:55,739
in a single Kingfisher case.

724
00:48:55,739 --> 00:48:59,511
The victims include Chairman Cheon,
head of a major Gangwon construction firm,

725
00:48:59,511 --> 00:49:02,326
and Mr. Tak, the son of a five-term lawmaker.

726
00:49:02,326 --> 00:49:04,379
The two men were together
in Chairman Cheon's room

727
00:49:04,379 --> 00:49:06,643
when a single bullet
fired from outside the window

728
00:49:06,643 --> 00:49:10,659
- instantly killed them both.
- Chairman Cheon is Cheon Seong Gil, right?

729
00:49:10,659 --> 00:49:12,271
This can't be happening.

730
00:49:12,271 --> 00:49:13,859
What's all this?

731
00:49:13,859 --> 00:49:16,326
And who's this Mr. Tak
who was killed with him?

732
00:49:16,326 --> 00:49:17,919
Accordingly, the sniper's point of origin...

733
00:49:17,919 --> 00:49:19,492
It's someone I know.

734
00:49:19,492 --> 00:49:20,692
Pardon?

735
00:49:20,692 --> 00:49:23,592
Do you know him? Who is he?

736
00:49:23,592 --> 00:49:27,407
The son of Assemblyman Tak Geun Soo,
Tak Jong Gu.

737
00:49:27,407 --> 00:49:30,967
Given the low-lying hills
outside the windows,

738
00:49:30,967 --> 00:49:33,859
investigators will need to determine

739
00:49:33,859 --> 00:49:35,859
- where Kingfisher carried out the attack.
- Ah, I wanted a chicken leg,

740
00:49:35,859 --> 00:49:37,019
but they're already sold out.

741
00:49:37,019 --> 00:49:38,759
They're really popular these days.

742
00:49:38,759 --> 00:49:42,135
Instead, I got you this fish cake bar
and the cream bread you like.

743
00:49:42,135 --> 00:49:43,995
And I got two sweet Choco Pies.

744
00:49:43,995 --> 00:49:45,227
Here you go!

745
00:49:45,227 --> 00:49:46,927
And some hot coffee!

746
00:49:47,979 --> 00:49:50,926
You were always lecturing me about
not using my phone while we're on stakeout.

747
00:49:50,926 --> 00:49:52,475
So what could be so interesting?

748
00:49:52,475 --> 00:49:54,175
Shh!

749
00:49:56,326 --> 00:49:58,155
[Two Victims Shot with a Single Bullet]

750
00:49:58,155 --> 00:50:01,292
What's this? Kingfisher struck again already?

751
00:50:03,643 --> 00:50:04,955
Two people?

752
00:50:04,955 --> 00:50:06,583
With one bullet?

753
00:50:06,583 --> 00:50:08,219
So, what is it? One shot, two kills?

754
00:50:08,219 --> 00:50:11,259
- Amazing!
- Hey, you're making a racket.

755
00:50:12,239 --> 00:50:13,239
Where are we going?

756
00:50:13,239 --> 00:50:15,395
We're in the middle of a stakeout, aren't we?

757
00:50:15,395 --> 00:50:18,071
Mr. Jang is going to take over.
He'll be here soon.

758
00:50:18,071 --> 00:50:20,643
Oh, so where are we...

759
00:50:20,643 --> 00:50:21,692
[Hongseon Casino]
Hongseon?

760
00:50:21,692 --> 00:50:24,299
A casino? At this hour?

761
00:50:24,299 --> 00:50:26,523
If we want to get footage of the scene,
we have to go now.

762
00:50:26,523 --> 00:50:27,587
Get some sleep.

763
00:50:27,587 --> 00:50:29,811
Wow, the scene of a one-shot double kill.

764
00:50:29,811 --> 00:50:33,592
But if the chief finds out about this,
we'll just get yelled at, right?

765
00:50:45,879 --> 00:50:48,531
[Five Years Ago]
The defendant, Tak Jong Gu,

766
00:50:48,531 --> 00:50:50,892
was found not guilty.

767
00:50:53,192 --> 00:50:56,207
Good work. Why did it take so long?

768
00:50:56,207 --> 00:50:57,635
No, this is unbelievable.

769
00:50:57,635 --> 00:51:01,679
How can there be a verdict like this?

770
00:51:01,679 --> 00:51:03,483
- Mom...
- My daughter is dead!

771
00:51:03,483 --> 00:51:05,426
- My sister...
- That punk killed her!

772
00:51:05,426 --> 00:51:07,967
- Mom!
- Hey!

773
00:51:07,967 --> 00:51:09,667
Mom...

774
00:51:11,467 --> 00:51:12,467
Bring my daughter back!

775
00:51:12,467 --> 00:51:15,439
How can he be found not guilty?

776
00:51:15,439 --> 00:51:18,392
Bring my daughter back!

777
00:51:18,392 --> 00:51:20,959
- Hey!
- Bring her back!

778
00:51:20,959 --> 00:51:22,975
- I said bring my daughter back!
- Mom...

779
00:51:22,975 --> 00:51:25,359
Bring my daughter back!

780
00:51:27,159 --> 00:51:29,792
[Court]

781
00:51:31,787 --> 00:51:34,926
Hey, get everyone together right now.

782
00:51:34,926 --> 00:51:37,963
What do you think? A celebration, you idiot.

783
00:51:37,963 --> 00:51:39,807
The girls?

784
00:51:39,807 --> 00:51:43,419
Of course, we should invite them.

785
00:51:43,419 --> 00:51:45,159
Yeah.

786
00:51:45,159 --> 00:51:46,335
Oh, really?

787
00:51:46,335 --> 00:51:49,026
Then should we just rent out an entire club?

788
00:51:51,827 --> 00:51:53,592
Let's go!

789
00:52:32,919 --> 00:52:35,859
Oh, Bo Na, Bo Na!

790
00:52:37,815 --> 00:52:40,103
Tae Seong!

791
00:52:40,103 --> 00:52:41,403
What brings you here at this hour?

792
00:52:41,403 --> 00:52:43,639
I came because I missed you.

793
00:52:43,639 --> 00:52:49,692
I just really wanted
to see you tonight, Bo Na.

794
00:52:53,027 --> 00:52:55,359
Have you been drinking?

795
00:52:55,359 --> 00:52:57,939
Well... a little?

796
00:52:57,939 --> 00:53:00,175
What...

797
00:53:00,175 --> 00:53:03,031
Why did you drink so much?
You can't even hold your liquor.

798
00:53:03,031 --> 00:53:05,527
That's not true. I can hold my liquor, okay?

799
00:53:05,527 --> 00:53:06,527
Tch...

800
00:53:06,527 --> 00:53:13,151
Still, I'd rather have
a strawberry shake with you.

801
00:53:13,151 --> 00:53:16,659
Cheers! Your favorite strawberry shake.

802
00:53:21,147 --> 00:53:26,175
But today, I just... drank like this.

803
00:53:26,175 --> 00:53:31,359
I drank because the only thing
I could hold in my hand

804
00:53:32,243 --> 00:53:33,951
was a glass of alcohol.

805
00:53:33,951 --> 00:53:38,807
Not a gun, not a knife, not even a pen.

806
00:53:38,807 --> 00:53:42,292
So I ended up with a glass.

807
00:53:49,351 --> 00:53:52,699
Did something happen today?

808
00:53:52,699 --> 00:53:54,751
Something?

809
00:53:54,751 --> 00:53:57,067
Well, yeah...

810
00:53:57,067 --> 00:53:59,679
Something always happens.
It's an everyday thing.

811
00:53:59,679 --> 00:54:01,767
Getting slammed into walls,

812
00:54:01,767 --> 00:54:04,826
thrown to the floor,

813
00:54:05,895 --> 00:54:09,863
and having my heart...

814
00:54:09,863 --> 00:54:12,626
ripped apart?

815
00:54:15,826 --> 00:54:18,492
I don't know what else I'm supposed to do.

816
00:54:23,026 --> 00:54:26,226
Bad people should be punished.

817
00:54:27,763 --> 00:54:30,992
Truly bad people should be punished.

818
00:54:33,959 --> 00:54:35,659
But I...

819
00:54:43,519 --> 00:54:46,326
I can't do anything about it.

820
00:55:24,463 --> 00:55:26,583
Get some sleep on the way.

821
00:55:26,583 --> 00:55:29,292
What are you thinking about so hard?

822
00:55:29,292 --> 00:55:31,327
Oh, nothing.

823
00:55:31,327 --> 00:55:33,795
I was just thinking about a certain day.

824
00:55:33,795 --> 00:55:35,719
What day?

825
00:55:35,719 --> 00:55:38,192
The day my husband cried for the second time.

826
00:55:42,903 --> 00:55:45,331
Well, aren't you tired yourself?

827
00:55:45,331 --> 00:55:49,823
I told you and Manager Go
to take a day off. I can drive.

828
00:55:49,823 --> 00:55:54,147
Ms. Yoo, how could I let you go alone?

829
00:55:54,147 --> 00:55:56,459
Driving at night is dangerous.

830
00:55:59,563 --> 00:56:02,919
Oh, no... I know you're...

831
00:56:02,919 --> 00:56:05,092
an excellent driver.

832
00:56:05,715 --> 00:56:08,226
But still, today...

833
00:56:08,226 --> 00:56:09,926
What about today?

834
00:56:11,715 --> 00:56:14,319
I just couldn't bring myself
to leave you alone.

835
00:56:14,319 --> 00:56:18,027
After the scare we had earlier.

836
00:56:18,027 --> 00:56:19,859
Especially since it was because of me.

837
00:56:20,535 --> 00:56:22,726
Hey, I told you it wasn't your fault.

838
00:56:22,726 --> 00:56:25,426
Unexpected things can happen anytime.

839
00:56:27,526 --> 00:56:29,631
It was the first time, Ms. Yoo.

840
00:56:29,631 --> 00:56:32,626
The first time I was truly scared.
Especially while I was there on-site.

841
00:56:34,403 --> 00:56:36,259
Me too.

842
00:56:36,259 --> 00:56:39,092
I was scared for the first time.

843
00:56:44,175 --> 00:56:47,043
Is this because you saw your husband today?

844
00:56:47,043 --> 00:56:49,659
You seemed bothered by it the whole time.

845
00:56:50,326 --> 00:56:53,392
Why did I never think of it?

846
00:56:54,055 --> 00:56:57,026
That something like this could happen.

847
00:57:36,775 --> 00:57:39,659
It's Yoo Bo Na, my wife.

848
00:57:41,079 --> 00:57:43,359
My big precious.

849
00:57:43,359 --> 00:57:46,259
Sorry, I woke you, right?

850
00:57:47,327 --> 00:57:50,619
I thought you'd be staying the night.

851
00:57:50,619 --> 00:57:53,095
I came back early because I missed you.

852
00:57:53,095 --> 00:57:55,926
I really missed you today.

853
00:57:59,527 --> 00:58:02,526
I missed you so much too.

854
00:58:05,755 --> 00:58:09,435
I'm off tomorrow. Want to go on a date?

855
00:58:09,435 --> 00:58:11,283
Let's do that.

856
00:58:11,283 --> 00:58:15,226
Let's have the date we missed last time.

857
00:58:15,931 --> 00:58:18,859
We'll look at the sky and enjoy the scenery.

858
00:58:20,407 --> 00:58:24,126
We'll worry about what to wear
and what to eat.

859
00:58:26,723 --> 00:58:30,383
Let's just have
an ordinary day together, okay?

860
00:58:30,383 --> 00:58:32,992
Just like the day we first met.

861
00:58:34,319 --> 00:58:36,892
Just like the day we first met.

862
00:58:48,419 --> 00:58:50,555
Why didn't I think of that?

863
00:58:50,555 --> 00:58:53,015
That he's always out there,

864
00:58:53,015 --> 00:58:55,067
and as long as I'm still here,

865
00:58:55,067 --> 00:59:00,292
we could run into each other again
someday, somewhere.

866
00:59:07,559 --> 00:59:09,292
Just like...

867
00:59:09,292 --> 00:59:12,392
the day we first met.

868
00:59:56,492 --> 00:59:58,735
Back then, everyone was curious
when you came back.

869
00:59:58,735 --> 01:00:00,403
They wondered what had happened
in the meantime.

870
01:00:00,403 --> 01:00:02,359
I met Yoo Bo Na.

871
01:00:02,359 --> 01:00:03,727
Try to stay alive, at least.

872
01:00:03,727 --> 01:00:05,692
Did you save Mr. Kwon Tae Seong?

873
01:00:05,692 --> 01:00:06,692
Because I felt like it.

874
01:00:06,692 --> 01:00:08,755
Have we met before?

875
01:00:08,755 --> 01:00:12,599
How do you keep picking out exactly
the people Kingfisher targets?

876
01:00:12,599 --> 01:00:14,963
But when I think about it,
she's really something.

877
01:00:14,963 --> 01:00:16,879
How on earth has she lived her life?

878
01:00:16,879 --> 01:00:17,975
Do you know anything, Tae Seong?

879
01:00:17,975 --> 01:00:21,471
Why would Director Yoo summon us
to her home herself?

880
01:00:21,471 --> 01:00:22,519
Wait a minute.

881
01:00:22,519 --> 01:00:25,859
Could Kingfisher have killed
an innocent person by mistake?

882
01:00:25,859 --> 01:00:28,279
If an innocent person was killed,
they should be held accountable too.

883
01:00:28,279 --> 01:00:30,092
Kingfisher should be caught
and locked up too.

884
01:00:30,092 --> 01:00:32,199
I got a text from Director Yoo.

885
01:00:32,199 --> 01:00:33,251
What did she say?

886
01:00:33,251 --> 01:00:34,599
I'm quitting.

887
01:00:34,599 --> 01:00:36,659
You used to want so badly to meet Kingfisher.

888
01:00:36,659 --> 01:00:38,592
I shouldn't meet her.

889
01:00:46,516 --> 01:00:48,516
Mkv Drama
